    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "FOR SALE VIA DIGITAL AUCTION 24TH SEPTEMBER 2026 FROM 11 AM \r\nAuction Registration, Legal Pack, and Viewing Times are available on the OFFR app on the link below \r\nhttps://artis.ie/properties/apartment-14-the-stockyard-the-steelworks-dublin-1/\r\n\r\nUpcoming Open Viewings: \r\n16 Sept, 17:30 - 17:45\r\n\r\nArtis is delighted to introduce to the market this third floor two-bedroom property. Extending to 61.71 sq. m/ 664 sq. ft, this apartment offers the opportunity to acquire an excellent investment or home in the heart of Dublin’s north inner city close to a myriad of amenities. Throughout the property there are generous proportions.\r\nUpon entering the apartment, one is welcomed by a generous hall leading to all the principal rooms. There is a spacious open plan kitchen/dining living area overlooking the central courtyard. The main bedroom is ensuite and there is a second double bedroom which opens to a generous steel balcony overlooking the central courtyard. The accommodation is completed by a guest bathroom and spacious storeroom with immersion tank, and boiler cupboard.\r\nThe Steelworks of which The Stockyard is a part is a modern apartment development in the heart of the North City Centre. The ground floor of the development is occupied by several businesses including Independent College a third level private college and Citas College Dublin and English Language School.  The development is located close to the IFSC and docklands with occupiers including the Central Bank, NTMA, PwC, A&L Goodbody, Salesforce, Citibank & Morgan Stanley. The 3 Arena, Convention Centre, Bord Gais Theatre and Point Village / Square (Odeon Cinema, Dunnes Stores, Starbucks) as well as a host of bars, restaurants and cafes are all just a short stroll or LUAS ride from the property to the North Docklands area. The location has the fabulous combination of being a in central location and having excellent transport links, with Connolly Train Station & LUAS Stop (Red Line) just 300m from the apartment and Docklands Train Station a 10min walk away. Dublin Port Tunnel provides access to the M50 and just a 15 min drive to the M50 / M1 junction or a 20min drive to Dublin Airport.\r\n\r\nMANAGEMENT COMPANY:\r\nSteelworks (FS2) Management CLG\r\n\r\nSERVICE CHARGE:\r\nApprox. €2,891 per annum. \r\n\r\nBER DETAIL:\r\nBER Rating: B3\r\nBER Number: 116316183\r\nEnergy Performance: 133.13 kWh/m²/yr\r\n\r\nSOLICITOR\r\nConor Dunne\r\nFieldfisher LLP\r\nFieldfisher Ireland LLP\r\n45 Mespil Road, Dublin 4\r\nD04 W2F1\r\nIreland"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Hall\r\nLaminate floor, intercom, fuse board, ceiling lights.\r\n\r\nBoiler room\r\nGas boiler\r\n\r\nStore room\r\nImmersion tank, immersion timer, ceiling light\r\n\r\nBathroom\r\nTiled floor and part tiled walls, bath, w.c, wall hung sink, ceiling light, extractor fan, shaving light.\r\n\r\nKitchen/living area\r\nLaminate floor, recessed lighting, built in wall and floor units, tiled splash back, oven, gas four ring hob, stainless steel extractor fan, stainless steel sink with draining board, heating control, 70:30 fridge freezer, washer/dryer,\r\n\r\nBedroom 1\r\nCarpet, ceiling light, built in wardrobe. \r\n\r\nEnsuite\r\nTiled floor and part tiled walls, ceiling light, shaving light, wall mounted sink, w.c, shower, extractor fan.\r\n\r\nBedroom 2\r\nCarpet, ceiling light, built in wardrobe, access to balcony.\r\n\r\nBalcony\r\nSpacious balcony with steel balustrade."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "•\tModern 2-bedroom apartment\r\n•\tVacant Possession, no rent cap.\r\n•\tExtending to circa 61.71 sq. m/ 664 sq. ft\r\n•\tExcellent B3 BER rating\r\n•\tLift to all floors and car park\r\n•\tSituated on the 3rd floor\r\n•\tGas fired central heating\r\n•\tDesignated parking space\r\n•\tWalking distance (3 mins) to Connolly Train Station & Luas Red Line Stop (4 mins)\r\n•\tLocated within close proximity to amenities around O’Connell Street \r\n•\tFor Sale via Digital Auction on 24th September 2026"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "BER Details",
        "SortOrder": 4,
        "Content": "BER: B3"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Directions",
        "SortOrder": 5,
        "Content": "Traveling from Connolly Station; Head north on Amiens Street toward Talbot Street. Turn left onto Talbot St and then right onto James Joyce Street. After 50m turn right onto Foley Street. The Steelworks will be on your left after approximately 230m. Please come into the central courtyard of the development."
      }
